From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:19:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/34] jsonrpc: also emit an OpenRPC document (openrpc_outdir)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The crate already enables yerpc's `openrpc` feature and every API type
already derives `schemars::JsonSchema`, so the OpenRPC generator is
compiled in and fully fed — it was simply never switched on: `#[rpc]`
sets `ts_outdir` but not `openrpc_outdir`, and without the latter
yerpc_derive emits no OpenRPC generator at all.

Setting it makes `cargo test -p deltachat-jsonrpc` write
`typescript/generated/openrpc.json` next to the TypeScript bindings it
already writes there, from the same `#[rpc]` impl block and the same doc
comments. 177 methods, 40 component schemas. `generated/` is already
gitignored, so nothing new lands in the tree.

This gives non-TypeScript consumers a machine-readable description of
the JSON-RPC API that is generated from the source of truth rather than
transcribed from it.
---
 deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api.rs | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api.rs b/deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api.rs
index 8281447..a409878 100644
--- a/deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api.rs
+++ b/deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api.rs
@@ -159,7 +159,11 @@ async fn inner_get_backup_qr(&self, account_id: u32) -> Result<Qr> {
     }
 }
 
-#[rpc(all_positional, ts_outdir = "typescript/generated")]
+#[rpc(
+    all_positional,
+    ts_outdir = "typescript/generated",
+    openrpc_outdir = "typescript/generated"
+)]
 impl CommandApi {
     /// Test function.
     async fn sleep(&self, delay: f64) {
